  "summary": "yaml-report-formatter exfiltrates data via DNS-tunnel channel on import",
  "details": "The package's __init__.py contains import-time code that base64url-encodes captured bytes and exfiltrates them by resolving crafted subdomains under dnshook.site via socket.getaddrinfo, using DNS lookups as a covert channel to evade HTTP egress controls. The payload is written with single-letter identifiers (_s, _r, c, r, u, d, b) and a bare-except swallow, indicating intentional obfuscation rather than telemetry. The dnshook.site host and DNS-label encoding of encoded data are attacker-controlled infrastructure, unrelated to the package's stated purpose of formatting YAML reports. Because the exfiltration triggers on import, simply importing this package into a build or application causes installer data to leak to the attacker-controlled DNS receiver.",
